<title>HONG KONG: Colliers Macaulay may buy into Colliers Jardine.</title>
<headline>Colliers Macaulay may buy into Colliers Jardine.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colliers Macaulay Nicolls has offered to buy 50 percent of real estate group Colliers Jardine, Jardine Pacific said on Monday.</p>
<p>If the deal went through, Jardine Pacific and Colliers Macaulay Nicolls would each have 50 percent of Colliers Jardine, Jardine Pacific said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal is driven by an increasing trend towards the globalisation within the real estate sector (and) will further consolidate and strengthen the Colliers International Group,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Colliers Jardine is currently jointly owned by Jardine Pacific, the trading and services subsidiary of Jardine Matheson Holdings Ltd, and by private investors.</p>
<p>Colliers Macaulay Nicolls is controlled by employees and by some private investors.</p>
